From: Alex Ayars <aayars@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 02:07:50 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 26/29] executor: close the MRT branch around the scatter/typed
 single-output path

Cherry-picking the iteration-group wiring onto the MRT dispatch merged
without conflict markers but dropped the brace that closes the MRT branch's
else, so executor.cpp no longer compiled. The scatter branch also lost its
outputTex bookkeeping in the same merge and sets wrote_output_tex again.
Native suite: 601 passed, 0 failed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EU6jaFnvpzrcsgg8pXrwK2
---
 src/graph/executor.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/graph/executor.cpp b/src/graph/executor.cpp
index 4b2c450..bde3282 100644
--- a/src/graph/executor.cpp
+++ b/src/graph/executor.cpp
@@ -3498,6 +3498,7 @@ ExecutionResult GraphExecutor::execute(const ExecutionPlan& plan,
               auto& stored = arena.insert(output_route, std::move(destination),
                                           format, ResourceLifetime::transient);
               effect_output = &stored;
+              wrote_output_tex = output_route == "outputTex";
               ++pass_count;
             } else {
             auto bindings = materialize_uniform_bindings(step, admission, pass,
@@ -3523,6 +3524,7 @@ ExecutionResult GraphExecutor::execute(const ExecutionPlan& plan,
             wrote_output_tex = output_route == "outputTex";
             ++pass_count;
             }
+            }
           } catch (const GraphError& error) {
             release_borrowed();
             if (error.effect_id().empty()) {
